// sets: A \ (A \ B) = A intersect B, double containment
let A, B be sets. wts A \ (A \ B) = A intersect B
let x in A \ (A \ B). then x in A and x not in A \ B, so x in B.
thus x in A intersect B.
conversely let x in A intersect B. then x in A and x in B, so x not in A \ B.
hence x in A \ (A \ B).
by double containment qed
